Z||000000||puter2k||01-17-2001||07:26 PM||||I just bought an 88 GT in excelent condition. It only has 34K miles on it, with power everything. I'm going to build a kit car and wanted a clean chasis. This car is so clean I hate to cut it up for a stretch job. I might consider trading it, for one of your 88 GT's, with high miles, and a few thou. If interested, ( Make offer ) I live in South Florida and you can contact me at puter2k@bellsouth.net<P>Details--Red V6, Auto, Power windows, Power locks, Power mirrors, Tilt, Cruise, AC, Power Lumbar driver seat, Power trunk release, Sub woofer, AM FM Tape w/ EQ, Beige cloth interior, 4 New tires, New Alt. Only draw back is it doesn't have a rear wing, It came from the factory that way ( no holes in trunk ). <P>Power lumbar seat is only on drivers side! No Pic's maybe this week end. No T-Tops, No Sun roof, Has Gold Rims, and that is 34,000 Original Miles !<P>               ( MAKE OFFER )<BR>I only want an 88 GT 6 CYL Auto in trade !<BR>I was thinking of 5 thou. + your car !<P>SORRY ABOUT THE ERROR ABOUT POWER STEERING, I CORRECTED THIS ON AN UPDATE! THE CAR HAS A FACTORY POWER LUMBAR SEAT AND THEY ARE RARE, IT'S THE ONLY ONE I'VE SEEN. <p>[This message has been edited by puter2k (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||01-17-2001||08:14 PM||||There's no such thing as a power seat.  More than likely its the "lumbar" seat.  Go to <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.net</A>  and check out the seat section, then go to '88 Lumbar.  I would bet money that it looks just like that.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||puter2k||01-17-2001||08:44 PM||||I stand corrected on the power seat. Just FWI they adjust the lumbar, sides at chest level, and sides along the thighs.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RaeQwan||01-17-2001||08:47 PM||||five grand plus my car? not that I have a 88 GT, but still.. anyone here crazy?<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwansig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Predator||01-17-2001||09:54 PM||||Man I'm not meaning to down your car, but $5,000 + another car. That is expecting a whole lot even for a 88 GT in great shape. The car is only worth around $5,000 according to Kelly Blue books in the shape you are saying it's in, and that is retail not trade in. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||puter2k||01-19-2001||08:36 PM||||Try finding an 88 GT with 34000 miles on it for any price, then come talk to me about Kelly Blue Book. These guys are so busy bashing me, they forget they are so called "FIERO" lovers! I don't know where they come from, but from where I do, car lovers hate to see a good vehicle get trashed. I just offered them a car that they claim to love ( in pristine condition). All I'd end up with is a chasis for my project. I'm tempted to cut it up just to spite them!||||reg||1
Z||000006||RaeQwan||01-19-2001||09:03 PM||||puter2k.. you talk babble.. a 88 GT with 34k miles, worth 5grand + another car. no matter the condition, you're still out of your mind.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwansig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||01-19-2001||09:05 PM||||Bottom line, the only way you are going to get more then 7 or 8 grand is if you are willing to wait.  People willing to spend that much are rare, however the do exist.  I doubt you will get more then 9 thousand.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
