Z||000010||2xsess||01-19-2001||09:16 PM||||Richard, please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><BR>I have seen many low mileage 88GTs for the same or less than what you're valuing yours at($5000 + another 88GT/Formula). Yes, we're fiero lovers but we're not into getting taken when buying one. If you talk/email mrfiero I'm sure he has one that he's selling for the same amount or less that's in the same condition, as a matter of fact he has a silver one which is the 2nd rarest of them all in excellent condition for $4000 (with only 68,000) miles delivered anywhere in the lower 48 states.<P>So, perhaps some one would buy yours for the $5000 but I highly doubt you'll get someone to trade you a running 88GT/Formula for it. If you do congrats.<P>Cutting it up to spite people here is your perrogative. <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 01-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fformula88||01-20-2001||12:26 AM||||I don.t mean any disrespect, but I think 5K plus a trade of another 88GT is a little much.  I am sure for that kind of cash with some patience a low milage high quality 88GT can be found.  <P>I don't think anyone meant disrespect to you in there comments.  I can also assure you they do love Fieros and don't just claim to.  They are just trying to make the point that the people who frequent this board are not very likely to give up that much for your GT, regardless of its condition.  We've all seen and heard from people who have gotten Fieros in great condition for far less!   <P>As for the kit, are you going to do an engine swap for it?  If so, maybe you just need to find a Fiero that has engine problems but a good frame.  Good luck on the project!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000012||87GT||01-20-2001||12:59 AM||||Puter2, I was just wondering if you bought that car in The North Tampa or Pasco County, FL area.  I saw a Red 88GT with no wing and the exact same mileage on autotrader for $5500 or so.  Just curious. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000013||mrfiero||01-20-2001||12:59 AM||||Just an update......since no one who e-mailed me about my silver GT bought it I have decided to keep it myself.  <P>$4000 delivered for a 68K mile '88 GT is a pretty good deal (atleast I think so  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ), but I still couldn't sell it!<P>I want to stay out of this squabble, but selling a low mileage Fiero is a tough thing to do.  It really does take the right person to buy it and that can take some time.  It's easier to sell 20 $500 Fieros than one $10K Fiero.<P>I am probably one of those "right" people as I paid $10K for my black '88 GT (had 10K miles on it at the time).....I also spent $10K for my 231 mile silver '88 Formula.  I'm just not in the market for another low mileage Fiero, otherwise I'd be tempted to buy this red one.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Predator||01-20-2001||09:39 AM||||Sorry if I ticked you off with the Kelly blue book quoate. All I was wanting to show you was most people around here are not going to pay much more than what the retail value is on any Fiero, but some people will. I spent $8,000 on my 85 GT. Since then I have learned that I probably gave too much, but I love the car, and that is really all that matters in the end. You will probably be better off just keeping the car and buying a blown up 88 Fiero GT for $500.00 or so from someplace like kickhill, or if you really need to sell it to finance your project then take it to ebay. It will be hard to find someone here who just happens to have a 88 GT laying around with $5,000, and are looking to trade up. They would have already sunk the five grand into the 88 GT by now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. If you want to cut up your car that I presume you spent a crap load of money for then that's your business. As much as I hate to see a good car cut up it is your property, and you have the right to do what you want with it. If you have that kind of money to through around to buy a GT like this and then cut it up for a kit, then good luck with the kit, and let us know how it turns out.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
